{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5kwDt3sskoBPRHvjZnW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This is necessary to provide an appropriate error code when attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment. The error code is part of the API contract, consistent with existing SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND and SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS codes.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new endpoint:\n   ```kotlin\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): Shipment\n   ```\n   This method will:\n   - Call `repository.findById(shipmentId)` and throw `ResourceNotFoundException` if not found\n   - Check if the shipment status is CANCELLED and throw `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` if so\n   - If status is CREATED, create a new Shipment instance with CONFIRMED status and save it\n   - If status is already CONFIRMED, return it unchanged (idempotent)\n   - Return the shipment in all success cases\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add comprehensive tests:\n   - `confirms_a_created_shipment` — Creates CREATED shipment, confirms it, verifies status is now CONFIRMED\n   - `confirm_is_idempotent` — Confirms the same shipment twice, verifies second confirm succeeds and returns CONFIRMED\n   - `rejects_confirming_a_cancelled_shipment` — Sets up CANCELLED shipment directly, attempts confirm, expects 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED\n   - `rejects_confirming_nonexistent_shipment` — Attempts to confirm non-existent shipment, expects 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Could reuse `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` for the CANCELLED rejection, but this is semantically wrong (the shipment exists, but in wrong state) and breaks the API contract's clarity. Each error condition should have its own code.\n- Could avoid adding an error code and use a generic validation error, but this doesn't follow the existing pattern where ConflictException has specific error codes.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Flow |\n|------|------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | GET from repo → new Shipment with CONFIRMED → save → return |\n| Already CONFIRMED | GET from repo → status check → return unchanged |\n| CANCELLED | GET from repo → status check → throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED) → 409 response |\n| Not found | GET from repo returns null → throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) → 404 response |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- **confirms_a_created_shipment**: Verifies the core happy path (status: CREATED → CONFIRMED)\n- **confirm_is_idempotent**: Verifies retry safety (second confirm of CONFIRMED shipment succeeds)\n- **rejects_confirming_a_cancelled_shipment**: Verifies business rule (CANCELLED is terminal)\n- **rejects_confirming_nonexistent_shipment**: Verifies error handling consistency (matches GET behavior)\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":806,"cache_read_input_tokens":20504,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":806},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b8e4f1b-757f-40e5-8bc5-a689ad1ec317","uuid":"aa50052b-44f5-4a9d-a392-bbe1ecf81c2a","timestamp":"2026-09-15T19:14:10.407Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5kwDSkVswMCZKSK8fPz"}
